diff --git a/docs/resume-session-actions.md b/docs/resume-session-actions.md
--- a/docs/resume-session-actions.md
+++ b/docs/resume-session-actions.md
@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Resume Session Actions
 
+- The resume picker displays directory filters in `Cwd`, `Other`, `All` order.
+- `Cwd` is the default unless the caller explicitly selects all sessions or has no cwd candidate.
+- Left selects the previous option and right selects the next option, wrapping at either end.
+- The same directional navigation applies to the `Updated`, `Created`, `Messages` sorting choices.
+- `Other` lists sessions outside the existing `Cwd` scope, within the selected active or archived status and provider.
+- Local linked worktrees with the same repository-relative cwd stay in the `Cwd` scope and are excluded from `Other`.
+- `Other` displays the session directory in the first field unless `Messages` sorting takes precedence.
+- Dense rows share a content-sized first column that uses available space before truncating paths and keeps titles aligned.
+- Directory exclusion is applied by the app-server before pagination.
+- Remote paths are resolved by that server, not the client's filesystem.
+- Search, sorting and profile actions keep the selected scope.
+- Without a cwd candidate, only `All` is available.
+- The fork picker retains its existing `Cwd` and `All` choices.
 - In the active-session list, Ctrl+A archives the selected session and keeps the picker open.
 - In the archived-session list, Enter performs `restore and resume`.
 - In the archived-session list, Ctrl+A performs `restore` without entering the session.
